title: Union - Party affairs
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
new-page: true
view-if: union_party_affairs_timer <= 0
card-image: img/labor_party.png
face-image: img/labor_party.png
on-arrival: union_party_affairs_timer += 8

= Union - party affairs

Allgemeiner Deutscher Gewerkschaftsbund / General German Trade Union Federation or better known as ADGB, is our associated umbrella of trade unions and alongside with them, we form two pillars of **Social Democracy**. Despite our deep ties, they are not bound to our policies and yield their own principles, as far as even accepting members of KPD and other radical socialist parties.

What should we do?

- @influence_adgb: Influence ADGB's policies.
- @influence_spd: Unions pressure us to do their biding.
- @return: Leave
- @easy_discard

@influence_spd
subtitle: Labor has gotten considerably strong and with their resistance, they require more control and voice in the matter of party politics.
view-if: labor_strength >= 35 and labor_dissent >= 30
on-arrival: labor_strength += 15; labor_dissent -= 20; center_dissent += 20; center_strength -= 20; reformist_dissent += 10; reformist_strength -= 10

ADGB has installed some of their representatives. 

@influence_adgb
subtitle: We promised to not intervene in ADGB's affairs outside of political coordination. 
view-if: labor_strength <= 34 and labor_dissent < 30
on-arrival: labor_strength -= 10; labor_dissent += 10

We have influenced ADGB to align with our policies. Union members are, obviously, pissed off at such intervention.